    <h2>How rows are chosen</h2>
    <p>The tracker lists general-purpose language models with public weights. It leaves out hosted-only products, image and speech models, and quantized copies. A row is added only after its facts are read on the repository; announcements and third-party summaries are not used as sources.</p>
    <p>Licenses differ inside one model family, so each row names the license of that repository. A custom license name means the terms are specific to the release and need to be read in full.</p>
    <p>For releases that are not yet checked here, see the automatically refreshed <a href="/news.html">news page</a>.</p>
